{"word": "differently", "source": "freedictionaryapi", "data": {"word": "differently", "entries": [{"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "adverb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈdɪfɹəntli/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈdɪfəɹəntli/", "tags": []}], "forms": [{"word": "more differently", "tags": ["comparative"]}, {"word": "most differently", "tags": ["superlative"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "In a different way.", "tags": [], "examples": ["Things turned out differently from what I'd envisaged."], "quotes": [{"text": "I was (says Mr. Highmore) forcibly struck with the violence of its pulsation, so much so, that, if it had been differently situated, I should have considered it an aneurism of considerable magnitude.", "reference": "1815, “Critical Analysis of Recent Publications”, in The Medical and Physical Journal, volume 34:"}, {"text": "\"You see, gentlemen, I couldn't bear the look of him, there was something in him ignoble, impudent, trampling on everything sacred, something sneering and irreverent, loathsome, loathsome. But now that he's dead, I feel differently.\"\n\"How do you mean?\"\n\"I don't feel differently, but I wish I hadn't hated him so.\"\n\"You feel penitent?\"\n\"No, not penitent, don't write that. I'm not much good myself; I'm not very beautiful, so I had no right to consider him repulsive. That's what I mean. Write that down, if you like.\"", "reference": "1912, Fyodor Dostoevsky, translated by Constance Garnett, The Brothers Karamazov:"}, {"text": "Recent research in the field of sociolinguistics and related fields has shown that women and men speak differently.", "reference": "2007, Vanessa Leonardi, Gender and Ideology in Translation: Do Women and Men Translate Differently?:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "различно"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "другояче"}, {"language": {"code": "ca"